{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310702,"nonce":"niaZpjQsufNkzfR+sJ9o2g6jKtw=","title":"FIXED 49ab3938: loop-carried SIMD4f vacc.add mis-compiled (panic / Usize_add / VectorBinOp{i64}). ROOT = SSA register-id REUSE leaving a ...","message":"Bug: `nue/tests/q8` oracle (the Q8_0 pure-Haxe matmul kernel) mis-compiled the\nloop-carried SIMD4f accumulator `vacc = vacc.add(vd.mul(vs))` — first as a hard\npanic (llvm_jit_backend `into_int_value` on a `phi \u003c4 x float\u003e`), later (after\nthe first half of the fix) as a graceful `LLVM upgrade failed ... VectorBinOp(int)\nleft not a vector (vec_ty=I64) ... continuing on Cranelift`. Same kernel ran fine\nin llama-chat — CONTEXT-DEPENDENT.\n\n**TRUE ROOT CAUSE — SSA register-id REUSE poisons the class-name hint (hir_to_mir).**\n`hir_to_mir` computes a `receiver_class_hint` for instance-method dispatch from\n`find_receiver_class_name` / `register_class_hints` (a Register→String map). When\nan SSA register id is REUSED across values of different types, its stale class-name\nhint persists. Two opposite hazards, both live in the oracle (proven by the\n`[hint-origin]` probe printing raw arg0 type, resolved receiver_type, and the\npre-existing name hint):\n 1. `vacc.add` (receiver TAST type 547=SIMD4f, convert_type=Vector{F32,4}) inherited\n    a stale **\"rayzor_Usize\"** hint → arith-intercept gate `== SIMD4f` FAILED →\n    `.add()` fell through to name resolution → **Usize_add** (scalar int add on a\n    vector; I64 return forced a `cast i64 -\u003e \u003c4 x f32\u003e` → panic).\n 2. A legit **Usize.add** address-arith call (receiver type 585=Usize,\n    convert_type=I64) inherited a stale **\"rayzor_SIMD4f\"** hint → mis-routed INTO\n    the arith interception → `VectorBinOp{Add}` fed i64 operands → LLVM rejects.\n\n**THE FIX (hir_to_mir.rs ~13519, the receiver_class_hint computation):**\n`convert_type(receiver_type)` — the DECLARED TAST type — is the SOLE authority for\nSIMD-vector classification. If it IS a vector → that simd class wins unconditionally\n(kills hazard 1). If it is NOT → any SIMD class named by the name/register hint is\nstale and is DISCARDED (kills hazard 2; non-SIMD hints like a real Bytes/Usize pass\nthrough). Genuine chained-SIMD receivers whose HIR type is opaque (Dynamic) are still\nrecovered from the receiver REGISTER's type (Variable-gated fallback).\nDefense-in-depth in the arith interception (~13602): it now ALSO requires\n`convert_type(args[0].ty)` (the actual receiver operand) to classify as f32x4, and\nthe emitted `vec_ty` can never fall back to a scalar — a stale hint can never again\nbuild a VectorBinOp over non-vector operands.\n\n**VERIFIED:** oracle bit-exact (worst-rel=0 self AND vs-Rust) + reaches LLVM with\nZERO fallback lines; Qwen2.5-0.5B Q6_K ~99 tok/s and Llama-3.2-1B Q4_K_M ~79 tok/s,\nboth coherent + PURE HAXE (ffi=0). Oracle nue/tests/q8 (Main.hx + rayzor.toml) now\nCOMMITTED (was untracked).\n\nThe prior hunt (12 probes, 7 fixes-before-probe, all failed) chased the wrong layer.\nIts \"final\" conclusions (probes 11–12: \"vacc's receiver expr carries a WRONG Usize\nsymbol 2416 / the inliner remaps vacc to a 585-typed symbol / TAST type inference\ncollapses SIMD4f→Usize\") were **FALSE**. TAST is INNOCENT: this session's\n`[t2h-methodcall]` probe showed vacc lowers as sym **2255=SIMD4f.add** (the 1 correct\nhit), and the **78x \"sym=2416 Usize.add recv_ty=585\"** were LEGITIMATE address\narithmetic (bsAddr/aBase — genuinely Usize), NOT mistyped vacc. The old chronicle\nMISREAD those 78 as poisoned vacc references. The swap to Usize_add happens ENTIRELY\nin hir_to_mir's hint heuristic, downstream of a correct TAST.\nAlso FALSE leads (do not revisit): @:native(\"add\") collision between Usize.hx:51 and\nSIMD4f.hx:45 (real convention smell but NOT this bug — SIMD4f.add never reaches\nnative-name lookup; it's intercepted to VectorBinOp); resolve_method_symbol / the\nlone-name pools / resolve_function_id_with_qualified_fallback (all proven no-effect).\n\nTwo probes closed it after 12 flailed: (1) `[intercept-gate]` — print\n`receiver_class_hint`, `convert_type(receiver_type)`, `is_vec` right AT the arith\ninterception gate; it showed the gate firing for a Usize call (hint=SIMD4f) and\nmissing for vacc. (2) `[hint-origin]` — print raw `args[0].ty`, resolved\n`receiver_type`, convert_type, AND the pre-existing `name_reg_hint`; it showed\n`receiver_type` was CORRECT (585 / I64) and the **name_reg_hint was the stale\n\"rayzor_SIMD4f\"**. Instrument the DECISION SITE (the gate + its inputs), not the\nsymbol/type upstream. See [[feedback_verify_codegen_by_disasm]] /\n[[feedback_debug_at_head_not_timetravel]].\n\n`register_class_hints` / `find_receiver_class_name` returning STALE hints for reused\nSSA register ids is the underlying defect; this fix makes the DECLARED type override\nit for SIMD, but the same staleness benignly mislabels Usize receivers as \"Bytes\"\n(18 such in the oracle — harmless only because Bytes has no colliding arith path).\nDurable fix per [[feedback_fqn_first_resolution]]: clear a register's class hint when\nit is reassigned to a value of a different type, OR key dispatch on the declared type\nthroughout and delete the register-name hint heuristic. Land gated on oracle+Qwen+Llama.\nThe env-gated `RAYZOR_VECCALL_DIAG` debug commit (99783e73) that preceded this can be\nremoved as cleanup — the bug it hunted is closed.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_simd4f_phi_intvalue_panic` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}